    "summary": "Shukrullo Rahmatovich Mirsaidov (14 February 1939 – 2 November 2012) was a Soviet and Uzbek politician and the 1st Vice President of Uzbekistan from March 1990 until the abolishment of the office on 8 January 1992. Formerly mayor of Tashkent and a key ally of the first Uzbek President Islam Karimov, Mirsaidov had served as the last Chairman of the Council of Ministers (prime minister) of the Uzbek SSR (1990) and then as Vice President of Uzbekistan until Karimov abolished this office on 8 January 1992.",
